# TinyHTTP

A lightweight HTTP server built from scratch in C# using TCP networking.

This project was created to explore how web servers receive, interpret and respond to HTTP requests without relying on an existing web framework.

## Overview

TinyHTTP uses TCP sockets to communicate with clients and process HTTP requests.

The server receives raw data from a client connection, interprets the HTTP request, validates the request and generates an HTTP response.

The project focuses on understanding the relationship between TCP communication and HTTP and learning what happens underneath higher-level web frameworks.

## Current Features

- Create a TCP listener using `TcpListener`
- Accept incoming client connections
- Receive data through a network stream
- Convert received byte data into a readable request representation
- Parse HTTP request information
- Extract the HTTP request method, path and HTTP version
- Parse HTTP headers
- Perform basic request validation
- Handle supported request methods
- Provide basic request routing
- Generate HTTP responses
- Convert responses into bytes for transmission
- Send responses back to the client
- Perform network operations asynchronously
- Log server activity to the console

## Request Processing

The general request flow is:

```text
Client / Browser
       |
       v
TCP Listener
       |
       v
Client Connection
       |
       v
Network Stream
       |
       v
HTTP Request
       |
       v
Request Parsing
       |
       v
Request Validation
       |
       v
Routing / Processing
       |
       v
HTTP Response
       |
       v
Response Bytes
       |
       v
Client / Browser


