## Project Structure

The project separates different parts of request processing rather than placing all server functionality into a single operation.

The implementation includes structures for representing parsed requests, headers, validation results and HTTP responses.

This separation makes it easier to parse, validate and respond to requests independently.


## Example Request

A browser may send a request similar to:

   | GET /index.html HTTP/1.1
   | Host: example.com

TinyHTTP reads the request through the TCP connection, interprets the HTTP information, validates the request and generates an appropriate HTTP response.


## Project Status

Learning and portfolio project.

The current implementation focuses on understanding the fundamentals of TCP communication and HTTP request/response processing.


